rganization and will remain the team's coach after Aaron Rodgers' allegations, sources told NFL Network and ESPN.","published":"2026-11-26T00:27:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50597534/sources-mike-mccarthy-steelers-full-support","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Brooke Pryor","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"RB Derrick Henry in concussion protocol but Ravens expect him to play Sunday","description":"Ravens running back Derrick Henry was placed back into concussion protocol Wednesday, but he is expected to play Sunday at the Texans.","published":"2026-11-25T22:33:48.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50597502/henry-concussion-protocol-ravens-expect-play","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jamison Hensley","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Tyler Lacy","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyler_Lacy","description":"American football player (born 1999)","touched":"2026-11-25T21:17:59Z","intro":"Tyler Lacy (born November 10, 1999) is an American professional football defensive tackle for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Oklahoma State Cowboys. Lacy was selected by the Jacksonville Jaguars in the fourth round of the 2023 NFL draft.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Lacy was born on November 10, 1999, in Garland, Texas. He is a cousin of former National Football League (NFL) player Aaron Ross, a Super Bowl champion with the New York Giants. He attended Sachse High School, being a consensus three-star recruit, and committed to play college football at Oklahoma State after his graduation from the school."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As freshman in 2018, Lacy redshirted and saw no game action at Oklahoma State. The following year, he started all 10 games in which he appeared, missing three due to injury, totaling 20 tackles, including two for a loss, with one sack and two pass breakups. In 2020, he remained a starter and was named honorable mention all-conference after leading the team's defensive line with 32 tackles and eight TFLs, additionally posting four sacks and five quarterback hurries.\nLacy earned a second honorable mention all-conference selection in 2021, additionally being named to their first-team All-Academic squad as he posted 34 tackles, 11 for-loss, and 3.5 sacks. He also recorded eight hurries, the fifth-best in school history since they started tracking the statistic in 1982. His senior season in 2022 was cut short due to injury, and he finished it with 17 tackles, five quarterback hits and three sacks. Lacy finished his stint at Oklahoma State with 113 tackles, 30 for-loss and 11.5 sacks while appearing in 44 total games."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"JACKSONVILLE JAGUARS\nLacy was selected by the Jacksonville Jaguars in the fourth round (130th overall) of the 2023 NFL draft. He appeared in 15 games and posted 12 tackles and a pass deflection in his first season.\nOn August 26, 2025, Lacy was waived by the Jaguars as part of final roster cuts.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn August 27, 2025, Lacy was claimed off waivers by the Detroit Lions."}],"wikidataId":"Q117716061","family":[{"relation":"Relative","name":"Aaron Ross","description":"American football player (born 1982)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aaron_Ross"}],"social":{"x":"tylerlacy85","instagram":"tylerlacy85"}},"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4361861","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/L/LacyTy00.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/tyler-lacy/76836","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/tyler-lacy/10954","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tyler_Lacy"},"insights":["On the field for 33% of Detroit’s defensive snaps this season.","2026 cap number of $1.1M is the 36th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Drafted 130th overall in 2023 (round 4) by JAX."]}